Biolubricants, also known as bio-based lubricants, are derived from renewable sources such as vegetable oils (e.g., rapeseed, soybean, palm) and animal fats. They serve as sustainable alternatives to conventional petroleum-based lubricants, offering enhanced biodegradability, reduced toxicity, and lower carbon footprints. Key product categories include hydraulic fluids, engine oils, gear oils, and metalworking fluids.
